# Commits that are pure formatting churn — no behavioural change. `git blame`
# skips them so line history points at the commit that last changed the code,
# not the one that reindented it.
#
# Enable locally (once):
#
#     git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# GitHub applies this file automatically; no setup needed there.
#
# Only add commits that are *entirely* mechanical — a commit mixing formatting
# with real edits would hide those edits from blame.

